Here. Right? What if we optimally tune beta? You

00:59:44.367 --> 00:59:46.527
know, we can't actually do that. We don't know what coverage

00:59:46.527 --> 00:59:48.757
is. But suppose we want to know what the ceiling

00:59:49.057 --> 00:59:51.217
of performance is, and we see that this is square root

00:59:51.217 --> 00:59:52.977
of coverage. Times epsilon squared.

00:59:53.537 --> 00:59:55.957
And note that this is actually significantly better

