you can check the paper.

03:18:16.418 --> 03:18:18.498
This I feel like this work opens up

03:18:18.498 --> 03:18:20.868
more questions than it answers, so there's a lot of

03:18:20.868 --> 03:18:22.986
avenues for future work. So

03:18:22.987 --> 03:18:25.408
one immediate thing that we find very surprising

03:18:26.168 --> 03:18:28.327
is why even does seat conditioning work in the

03:18:28.327 --> 03:18:30.447
first place? So why is it that we're

03:18:30.448 --> 03:18:32.228
able to provide random strings

03:18:33.087 --> 03:18:35.348
and the model is learning what is the right structure

03:18:35.488 --> 03:18:37.698
to use this diversity to get

03:18:37.938 --> 03:18:40.018
these tasks. For example, the model is able to go from a

03:18:40.018 --> 03:18:42.038
random string to a stochastic plan of

03:18:42.038 --> 03:18:44.118
the parent or stochastic plan of

03:18:44.118 --> 03:18:46.518
which triangle to generate and so on. So

03:18:46.578 --> 03:18:48.738
why is it that this works? Like, how is the model able to

03:18:48.738 --> 03:18:51.008
do that? That's very surprising and something

03:18:51.008 --> 03:18:52.448
that's worth investigating.

03:18:53.728 --> 03:18:55.988
On the other side, I spoke about mode conditioning

03:18:56.048 --> 03:18:58.058
where we provide very clear

03:18:58.058 --> 03:19:00.398
semantically meaningful modes to the model.

03:19:00.688 --> 03:19:02.928
But then we don't have a way to get new random

03:19:02.928 --> 03:19:05.168
modes. So how do we get extrapolation?

03:19:05.628 --> 03:19:07.647
Can we prompt the model with, like, a mix

03:19:07.807 --> 03:19:09.887
mixture of modes in the prompt? And does that allow the

03:19:09.888 --> 03:19:11.918
model to actually generate, like, completely

03:19:11.918 --> 03:19:14.077
new strategy, for example? So can we get

03:19:14.077 --> 03:19:16.118
the best of what the model is able to do with

03:19:16.358 --> 03:19:18.777
seed conditioning, but also in a way that's more semantically

03:19:18.918 --> 03:19:21.017
meaningful so that might work even better?

03:19:21.138 --> 03:19:23.298
So that's another very interesting question to think

03:19:23.298 --> 03:19:23.538
about.

03:19:25.378 --> 03:19:27.718
And a lot of our contribution was hopefully

03:19:28.018 --> 03:19:30.448
to build minimal examples that can inspire

03:19:30.508 --> 03:19:32.557
new ideas. We wanted to first

03:19:32.557 --> 03:19:34.468
have a way to concretely think about

03:19:34.708 --> 03:19:36.788
creativity and show what we might be missing

03:19:36.788 --> 03:19:38.807
with our current models. And we

03:19:38.808 --> 03:19:40.888
came up with, like, few alternatives, and

03:19:40.888 --> 03:19:43.178
I think there's room for a lot lot more,

03:19:43.178 --> 03:19:45.118
lot better strategies for diversity,

03:19:45.398 --> 03:19:47.898
for training these models to allow them to infer

03:19:48.118 --> 03:19:50.358
this sort of unobserved creative

03:19:50.358 --> 03:19:52.438
leap of thought. So I hope you can all join us

03:19:52.438 --> 03:19:54.618
in developing new methods to further push

03:19:54.618 --> 03:19:56.398
this next frontier of these models.

03:19:57.388 --> 03:19:59.628
